{"questions":[{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077f3","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077f3","q":"<p>Find the principal value of `cot^-1 ((-1)/sqrt(3))`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let y = `cot^-1 ((-1)/sqrt(3))`</p>\n<p>Since, cot<sup>–1</sup>(– x) = π – cot<sup>–1</sup>x</p>\n<p>∴ y = `π - cot^-1 (1/sqrt(3))`</p>\n<p>⇒ y = `π - π/3`  ......`(∵ cot π/3 = 1/sqrt(3))`</p>\n<p>⇒ y = `(2π)/3`</p>\n<p>Since, range of cot<sup>–1</sup> is (0, π)</p>\n<p>Hence, principal value is `(2π)/3`.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077c7","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077c7","q":"<p>The principal solutions of cot x = -`sqrt3`  are .................</p>","options":["<p>`pi/6 ,(5pi)/6`</p>","<p>`(5pi)/6 , (7pi)/6`</p>","<p>`(5pi)/6,(11pi)/6`</p>","<p>`pi/6,(11pi)/6`</p>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>`(5pi)/6,(11pi)/6`<br/>cot x = `sqrt3`</p>\n<p>cot x = `-\"cot\"(pi/6) = cot(pi-pi/6) = \"cot\" (2pi - pi/6)`</p>\n<p>= `\"cot\"((5pi)/6) = cot ((11pi)/6)`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607889","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607889","q":"<p>In ΔABC if a = 13, b = 14, c = 15, then find the value of sec A.</p><br><br><p>In ΔABC if a = 13, b = 14, c = 15, then find the value of `\"cosec\" A/2`.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Using the cosine rule:</p>\n<p>cos A = `(b^2 + c^2 - a^2)/(2bc)`</p>\n<p>= `(14^2 + 15^2 - 13^2)/(2(14)(15))`</p>\n<p>= `(196 + 225 - 169)/420`</p>\n<p>= `252/420`</p>\n<p>= `3/5`</p>\n<p>sec A = `1/cos A`</p>\n<p>= `1/(3/5)`</p>\n<p>= `5/3`</p>\n<p>= 1.67</p><br><br><p>s = `(a + b + c)/2`</p>\n<p>= `(13 + 14 + 15)/2`</p>\n<p>= 21</p>\n<p>Using the half-angle formula: </p>\n<p>`sin  A/2 = sqrt(((s - b)(s - c))/(bc))`</p>\n<p>`sin  A/2 = sqrt(((21- 14)(21 - 15))/((14)(15)))`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt((7 xx 6)/(210))`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt(42/210)`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt(1/5)`</p>\n<p>= `1/sqrt5`</p>\n<p>`\"cosec\" A/2 = 1/(sin  A/2)`</p>\n<p>= `1/(1/sqrt5)`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt5`</p>\n<p>= 2.236</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607870","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607870","q":"<p>In ΔABC, (a + b) cos C + (b + c) cos A + (c + a) cos B is equal to ______.</p>","options":["<p>a − b + c</p>","<p>a + b − c</p>","<p>a + b + c</p>","<p>a − b − c</p>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>In ΔABC, (a + b) cos C + (b + c) cos A + (c + a) cos B is equal to <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>a + b + c</strong></span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>We know that in a triangle,</p>\n<p>cos A = `(b^2 + c^2 - a^2)/(2bc)`</p>\n<p>cos B = `(a^2 + c^2 - b^2)/(2ac)`</p>\n<p>cos C = `(a^2 + b^2 - c^2)/(2ab)`</p>\n<p>Now, substituting these values into the given equation:</p>\n<p>(a + b) cos C + (b + c) cos A + (c + a) cos B</p>\n<p>Expanding each term,</p>\n<p>`(a + b) xx (a^2 + b^2 - c^2)/(2ab) + (b + c) xx (b^2 + c^2 - a^2)/(2bc) + (c + a) xx (a^2 + c^2 - b^2)/(2ac)`</p>\n<p>By simplifying the expressions and using triangle properties, the result simplifies to: </p>\n<p>a + b + c</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860787d","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860787d","q":"<p>Find the general solution of tan<sup>2</sup>θ = 1.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>We have tan<sup>2</sup>θ = 1</p>\n<p>∴ `tan^2θ = tan^2  pi/4`</p>\n<p>The general solution of tan<sup>2</sup>θ = α is θ = nπ ± α, where n ∈ Z.</p>\n<p>∴ The general solution of tan<sup>2</sup>θ = `tan^2  pi/4` is θ = `npi ± pi/4`, where n ∈ Z.</p>\n<p>∴ The general solution of tan<sup>2</sup>θ = 1 is θ = `npi ± pi/4`, where n ∈ Z.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607844","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607844","q":"<p>The principle solutions of the equation cos θ = `1/2` are ______.</p>","options":["<p>`π/6, (5π)/6`</p>","<p>`π/3, (5π)/3`</p>","<p>`π/6, (7π)/6`</p>","<p>`π/3, (2π)/3`</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>The principle solutions of the equation cos θ = `1/2` are `bbunderline(π/3, (5π)/3)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>cos θ = `1/2`</p>\n<p>= cos `π/3`</p>\n<p>= `cos (2π - π/3)`</p>\n<p>= `cos  (5 pi)/3`</p>\n<p>∴ Principal solution: `pi/3, (5 pi)/3` ∈ (0. 2π)</p>\n<p>∴ `π/3, (5π)/3`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607851","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607851","q":"<p>In ΔABC, if a = 18, b = 24, c = 30 then find the values of sin `(A/2)`.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n<p>a = 18, b = 24 and c = 30</p>\n<p>∴ 2s = a + b + c</p>\n<p>= 18 + 24 + 30</p>\n<p>= 72</p>\n<p>∴ s = `72/2`</p>\n<p>∴ s = 36</p>\n<p>`sin  (A/2) = sqrt(((s - b)(s - c))/(bc)`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt(((36 - 24)(36 - 30))/((24)(30)`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt((12 xx 6)/(24 xx 30)`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt(1/10)`</p>\n<p>= `1/(sqrt10)`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607818","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607818","q":"<p><strong>Select the correct option from the given alternatives:</strong></p>\n<p>In ΔABC if c<sup>2</sup> + a<sup>2</sup> – b<sup>2</sup> = ac, then ∠B = ____.</p>","options":["<p>`π/4`</p>","<p>`π/3`</p>","<p>`π/2`</p>","<p>`π/6`</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>In ΔABC if c<sup>2</sup> + a<sup>2</sup> – b<sup>2</sup> = ac, then ∠B = `underlinebb(π/3)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>cos B = `(c^2 + a^2 - b^2)/(2ac)`</p>\n<p>cos B = `(ac)/(2ac)`</p>\n<p>cos B = `1/2`</p>\n<p>cos B = cos `pi/3`</p>\n<p>B = `pi/3`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607825","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607825","q":"<p><strong>Find the Cartesian co-ordinates of the point whose polar co-ordinates are:</strong></p>\n<p>`(sqrt(2), pi/4)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Here, r = `sqrt(2) and θ = pi/(4)`<br/>Let the cartesian coordinates be (x, y)</p>\n<p>Then, x = r cos θ = `sqrt(2)cos  pi/(4) = sqrt(2)(1/sqrt(2))` = 1</p>\n<p>y = r sin θ = `sqrt(2)sin  pi/(4) = sqrt(2)(1/sqrt(2))` = 1<br/>∴ the cartesian coordinates of the given point are (1, 1).</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077ec","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077ec","q":"<p><strong>Select the correct option from the given alternatives:</strong></p>\n<p>In ΔABC if c<sup>2</sup> + a<sup>2</sup> – b<sup>2</sup> = ac, then ∠B = ____.</p>","options":["<p>`π/4`</p>","<p>`π/3`</p>","<p>`π/2`</p>","<p>`π/6`</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>In ΔABC if c<sup>2</sup> + a<sup>2</sup> – b<sup>2</sup> = ac, then ∠B = `underlinebb(π/3)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>cos B = `(c^2 + a^2 - b^2)/(2ac)`</p>\n<p>cos B = `(ac)/(2ac)`</p>\n<p>cos B = `1/2`</p>\n<p>cos B = cos `pi/3`</p>\n<p>B = `pi/3`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077f9","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077f9","q":"<p>Find the principal solutions of cot θ = 0</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Given, cot θ = 0</p>\n<p>Since, cot θ ∈ (0, 2π)</p>\n<p>∴ cot θ = 0 = `cot  π/2 = cot(π + π/2)`  ......[∵ cot (π + θ) = cot θ]</p>\n<p>∴ cot θ = `cot  π/2 = cot  (3π)/2` </p>\n<p>∴ θ = `π/2` or θ = `(3π)/2`</p>\n<p>Hence, the required principal solutions are `{π/2, (3π)/2}`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077fc","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077fc","q":"<p>Find the cartesian co-ordinates of the point whose polar co-ordinates are `(1/2, π/3)`.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Here, r = `1/2` and θ = `π/3`</p>\n<p>Let the cartesian coordinates be (x, y).</p>\n<p>Then, x = r cos θ = `1/2 cos  π/3 = 1/2 xx 1/2 = 1/4`</p>\n<p>And y = r sin θ = `1/2 sin  π/3 = 1/2 xx sqrt(3)/2 = sqrt(3)/4`</p>\n<p>∴ The cartesian coordinates of the given point are `(1/4, sqrt(3)/4)`.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077a0","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077a0","q":"<p>The principal solutions of sec x = `2/sqrt3` are _____ </p>","options":["<p>`pi/3,(11pi)/6`</p>","<p>`pi/6, (11pi)/6`</p>","<p>`pi/4,(11pi)/4`</p>","<p>`pi/6,(11pi)/4`</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>sec x= `2/sqrt3`</p>\n<p>`cos x = sqrt3/2 = cos pi/6 = cos(2pi - pi6)`</p>\n<p>`pi/6, (11pi)/6`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607779","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607779","q":"<p>In Δ ABC, if a = 13, b = 14 and c = 15, then sin (A/2)= _______.</p>\n<p>(A) `1/5`</p>\n<p>(B) `sqrt(1/5)`</p>\n<p>(C) `4/5`</p>\n<p>(D) `2/5`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>(B) `sqrt(1/5)`</p>\n<p>`s=(a+b+c)/2=(13+14+15)/2=21`</p>\n<p>`sin(A/2)=sqrt(((s-b)(s-c))/(bc))=sqrt(((21-14)(21-15))/(14xx15))=sqrt(1/5)`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860777b","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860777b","q":"<p>In Δ ABC, prove that, a (b cos C - c cos B) = b<sup>2</sup> - c<sup>2</sup>.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Taking LHS<br/>`a(bcosC-c cosB)`</p>\n<p>`=abcosC-ac cosB`</p>\n<p>`=ab((a^2+b^2-c^2)/(2ab))-ac((a^2+c^2-b^2)/(2ac))`</p>\n<p>`(a^2+b^2-c^2-a^2-c^2+b^2)/2`</p>\n<p>`=(2b^2-2c^2)/2`</p>\n<p>`=b^2-c^2 \"(RHS)\"`</p>\n<p> </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607888","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607888","q":"<p>Prove that `2 tan^(-1) (1/3) + cos^(-1) (3/5) = pi/2`.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Using the double-angle formula for inverse tangent:</p>\n<p>L.H.S. = `2 tan^(-1) (1/3) + cos^(-1) (3/5)`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)[(2 xx 1/3)/(1 - 1/3^2)] + cos^(-1) (3/5)   ...[2tan^(-1)x = tan^(-1)((2x)/(1 - x^2))]`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)[(2 xx 1/3)/(1 - 1/3^2)] + tan^(-1)sqrt((1 - 9/25)/(3/5))    ...[cos^(-1)x = tan^(-1)(sqrt(1 - x^2)/x)]`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)[(2/3)/(1 - 1/9)] + tan^(-1)  sqrt(((25 - 9)/25)/(3/5))`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)[(2/3)/((9 - 1)/9)] + tan^(-1)sqrt((16/25)/(3/5))`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)((2/3)/(8/9)) + tan^(-1)((4/5)/(3/5))`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)(2/3) xx(9/8) + tan^(-1)(4/5) xx (5/3)`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)(3/4) + tan^(-1)(4/3)    ...[tan^(-1)a + tan^(-1)b = tan^(-1)((a + b)/(1 - ab))\", if \" ab &lt; 1]`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)((3/4 + 4/3)/(1 - (3/4 xx 4/3)))`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)(((9 + 16)/12)/(1 - 1))`</p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)(((25)/12)/(0))`     </p>\n<p>= `tan^(-1)(0)  ...(tan0° = pi/2)`</p>\n<p>= `pi/2`</p>\n<p>= R.H.S.</p>\n<p>L.H.S. = R.H.S.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860785c","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860785c","q":"<p><strong>Prove the following:</strong></p>\n<p>`tan^-1(1/2) + tan^-1(1/3) = pi/(4)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>L.H.S. = `tan^-1(1/2) + tan^-1(1/3)`</p>\n<p>= `tan^-1 [(1/2 + 1/3)/(1 - 1/2 * 1/3)]`    ...since `1/2 &gt; 0, 1/3 &gt; 0` and `(1/2)(1/3) &lt; 1`</p>\n<p>= `tan ^-1 ((5/6)/(1 - 1/6))`</p>\n<p>= `tan^-1((5/6)/(5/6))`</p>\n<p>= tan<sup>-1</sup>(1)</p>\n<p>= `tan^-1(tan  pi/4)`</p>\n<p>= `pi/(4)`</p>\n<p>= R.H.S.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860785d","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860785d","q":"<p><strong>In ΔABC, prove the following:</strong></p>\n<p>`(cos A)/a + (cos B)/b + (cos C)/c = (a^2 + b^2 + c^2)/(2abc)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>LHS = `(cos A)/a + (cos B)/b + (cos C)/c`</p>\n<p>`= (((\"b\"^2 + \"c\"^2 - \"a\"^2)/\"2bc\"))/\"a\" + (((\"c\"^2 + \"a\"^2 - \"b\"^2)/\"2ca\"))/\"b\" + (((\"a\"^2 + \"b\"^2 - \"c\"^2)/\"2ab\"))/\"c\"`</p>\n<p>`= (\"b\"^2 + \"c\"^2 - \"a\"^2)/\"2abc\" + (\"c\"^2 + \"a\"^2 - \"b\"^2)/\"2abc\" + (\"a\"^2 + \"b\"^2 - \"c\"^2)/\"2abc\"`</p>\n<p>`= (\"b\"^2 + \"c\"^2 - \"a\"^2 + \"c\"^2 + \"a\"^2 - \"b\"^2 + \"a\"^2 + \"b\"^2 - \"c\"^2)/\"2abc\"`</p>\n<p>`= (\"a\"^2 + \"b\"^2 + \"c\"^2)/\"2abc\"`</p>\n<p>= RHS</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860782f","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860782f","q":"<p>Find the general solution of sin θ + sin 3θ + sin 5θ = 0</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>We have sin θ + sin 3θ + sin 5θ = 0</p>\n<p>∴ (sin θ + sin 5θ) + sin 3θ = 0</p>\n<p>∴ 2 sin 3θ × cos 2θ + sin 3θ = 0</p>\n<p>∴ (2 cos 2θ + 1) sin 3θ = 0</p>\n<p>∴ sin 3θ = 0 or cos 2θ = `-1/2`</p>\n<p>∴ sin 3θ = 0 or cos 2θ = `cos  (2π)/3`</p>\n<p>∴ 3θ = nπ or 2θ = `2nπ ± (2π)/3`, where n ∈ Z.</p>\n<p>θ = `(nπ)/3` or θ = `nπ ± π/3`,</p>\n<p>where n ∈ Z is the required general solution.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607830","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607830","q":"<p>If –1 ≤ x ≤ 1, the prove that sin<sup>–1</sup> x + cos<sup>–1</sup> x = `π/2`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let sin<sup>–1</sup> x = θ, where x ∈ [–1, 1] and `θ ∈ [-π/2, π/2]`</p>\n<p>∴ `- θ ∈ [-π/2, π/2]`</p>\n<p>∴ `π/2 - θ ∈ [0, π]`, the principal domain of the cosine function.</p>\n<p>∴ `cos(π/2 - θ)` = sin θ</p>\n<p>`cos(π/2 - θ)` = x</p>\n<p>∴ cos<sup>–1</sup> x = `π/2 - θ`</p>\n<p>∴ `θ + cos^-1x = π/2`</p>\n<p>∴ sin<sup>–1</sup> x + cos<sup>–1</sup> x = `π/2`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607803","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607803","q":"<p>If 2 tan<sup>–1</sup>(cos x) = tan<sup>–1</sup>(2 cosec x). then find the value of x.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>As we know that</p>\n<p> 2 tan<sup>–1</sup>(x) = `tan^-1 ((2x)/(1 - x^2))`</p>\n<p>∴ 2 tan<sup>–1</sup>(cos x) = `tan^-1 ((2 cos x)/(1 - cos^2x))`</p>\n<p>⇒ 2 tan<sup>–1</sup>(cos x) = `tan^-1 ((2 cos x)/(sin^2x))`</p>\n<p>Given, 2 tan<sup>–1</sup> (cos x) = tan<sup>–1</sup> (2 cosec x)</p>\n<p>∴ `tan^-1 ((2 cos x)/(sin^2x))` = tan<sup>–1</sup> (2 cosec x)  ......[From (i)]</p>\n<p>⇒ `(2 cos x)/sin^2x `= 2 cosec x</p>\n<p>⇒ `cosx/sin^2x = 1/sinx`</p>\n<p>⇒ cos x = sin x</p>\n<p>⇒ x = `π/4`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077d6","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077d6","q":"<p> In , ΔABC prove that </p>\n<p>`\"sin\"((\"B\" - \"C\")/2) = ((\"b\" - \"c\")/\"a\") \"cos\"(\"A\"/2)`                               </p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>RHS = `((\"b\"-\"c\")/\"a\") \"cos\"\"A\"/2`         ...(by sine rule)</p>\n<p>=`((\"k\" \"sin\" \"B\" - \"k\" \"sin\" \"C\")/(\"k\" \"sin\"\"A\")) . \"cos\"\"A\"/2`</p>\n<p>= `[\"k\"[\"sin\"\"B\" - \"sin\"\"C\"]]/(\"k\"\"sin\"\"A\") .\"cos\"\"A\"/2`</p>\n<p>=`[[2\"cos\" (\"B\"+\"C\")/2 . \"sin\" (\"B\" -\"C\")/2]]/(2 \"sin\" \"A\"/2 \"cos\"\"A\"/2) . \"cos\"\"A\"/2` </p>\n<p>= `(2\"cos\" (pi/2-\"A\"/2) \"sin\"<br/>((\"B\"-\"C\")/2))/(2 \"sin\" \"A\"/2)`</p>\n<p>=` \"sin\"((\"B\"-\"C\")/2) = \"LHS\"`</p>\n<p>Hence, the required result is proved.                           </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077d7","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077d7","q":"<p>Show that `\"sin\"^-1(5/13) + \"cos\"^-1(3/5) = \"tan\"^-1(63/16)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let `\"sin\"^-1 (5/13) = \"A\" =&gt; \"sin\"\"A\" = 5/13`</p>\n<p>`therefore \"cos\"\"A\" = sqrt(1-\"sin\"^2\"A\") = sqrt(1-(5/13)^2)`</p>\n<p>`sqrt (1-25/169) = sqrt(144/169) = 12/13`</p>\n<p>`=&gt; \"tan\"\"A\" = 5/12`</p>\n<p>let `\"cos\"^-1(3/5) = \"B\" =&gt; \"cos\"\"B\" = 3/5 `</p>\n<p>sin B =`sqrt(1-9/25) = sqrt (16/25) = 4/5`</p>\n<p>`therefore \"tan\"\"B\" = 4/3`</p>\n<p>Now , tan (A + B) =` (\"tan\"\"A\" +\"tan\"\"B\")/(1 - \"tan\"\"A\"\"tan \" \"B\")`</p>\n<p>`=&gt; \"A\" + \"B\" = \"tan\"^-1 [[ 5/12 +4/3]/(1-5/12 xx 4/3)]`</p>\n<p>`= \"tan\"^-1 [[(5+16]/12)/( (36 - 20)/36]]`</p>\n<p>A +B = `\"tan\"^-1 [(21/16)/3]`</p>\n<p>`=&gt; \"sin\"^-1 (5/13) + \"cos\"^-1(3/5) = \"tan\"^-1(63/16)`</p>\n<p>= R.H.S </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607781","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607781","q":"<p>Find the general solution of the equation sin 2x + sin 4x + sin 6x = 0</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>`(sin 2x +sin 6x)+sin 4x =0`</p>\n<p>`2sin4x.cos2x+sin4x=0`</p>\n<p>`sin4x(2cos2x+1)=0`</p>\n<p>`sin 4x=0 or 2cos2x+1=0`</p>\n<p>`sin4x=0 or cos2x=-1/2=-cos  pi/3=cos(pi-pi/3)`</p>\n<p>Using `sinx=0=&gt;x=npi`</p>\n<p>`sin4x=0`</p>\n<p>`4x=npi`</p>\n<p>The genral solution is x</p>\n<p>`x=(npi)/4` </p>\n<p>using `cosx=cosalpha=&gt;x=2mx+-alpha`</p>\n<p>`cos2x=cos((2pi)/3)`</p>\n<p>`2x=2mpi+-(2pi)/3`</p>\n<p>The genral solution is x</p>\n<p>`x=mpi+-pi/3` where `m,n in z`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607787","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607787","q":"<p>Show that:</p>\n<p>`cos^(-1)(4/5)+cos^(-1)(12/13)=cos^(-1)(33/65)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let a = `\"cos\"^-1 (4/5)` and b = `\"cos\"^-1 (12/13)`</p>\n<p>Let a = `\"cos\"^-1 (4/5)`</p>\n<p>cos a = `4/5`</p>\n<p>We know that</p>\n<p>sin<sup>2</sup>a = 1 - cos<sup>2</sup>a </p>\n<p><br/>sin a = `sqrt (1-\"cos\"^2 \"a\")`</p>\n<p><br/>`= sqrt (1 - (4/5)^2) = sqrt (1 - 16/25)`</p>\n<p><br/>`= sqrt ((25-16)/25) = sqrt (9/25) = 3/5`</p>\n<p><br/>Let b = `\"cos\"^-1 (12/13)`</p>\n<p>cos b = `12/13`</p>\n<p>W know that</p>\n<p>sin<sup>2</sup>b = 1 - cos<sup>2</sup>b </p>\n<p><br/>sin b = `sqrt (1 - \"cos\"^2 \"b\")`</p>\n<p><br/>`= sqrt (1 - (12/13)^2) = sqrt (1 - 144/169)`</p>\n<p><br/>`= sqrt ((169-144)/169) = sqrt (25/169) = 5/13`</p>\n<p>We know that </p>\n<p>cos (a+b) = cos a cos b - sin a sin b</p>\n<p><strong>Putting values </strong></p>\n<p>cos a = `4/5` , sin a = `3/5`</p>\n<p>&amp; cos b = `12/13` , sin b = `5/13`</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>cos (a+b) = `4/5 xx 12/13 xx 3/5 xx 5/13`</p>\n<p><br/>`= 48/65 - 3/13`</p>\n<p><br/>`= (48 - 15)/65`</p>\n<p><br/>`= 33/65`</p>\n<p>∴ cos (a+b) = `33/65`</p>\n<p>a + b = cos<sup>-1</sup> `(33/65)`</p>\n<p>`\"cos\"^-1 4/5 + \"cos\"^-1 (12/15) = \"cos\"^-1 (33/65)`</p>\n<p>Hence LH.S = R.H.S</p>\n<p>Hence proved.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077e0","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077e0","q":"<p> In ,Δ ABC with usual notations prove that <br/>b<sup>2</sup> = c<sup>2</sup> +a<sup>2</sup> - 2 ca cos B</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p> Consider that for Δ ABC , ∠B is in a standard position i.e. vertex B is at the origin and the side BC is along positive x-axis. As ∠B  is an angle of a triangle ∴ ∠B can be acute or ∠B  can be obtuse.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afdbe3720f1c028af4f8.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afdbe3720f1c028af4f8.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afdbe3720f1c028af4f8.png?alt=media\"/></p>\n<p>Using the Cartesian co-ordinate system in above figure.</p>\n<p>we get B ≡(0,0) A ≡(c cos B , c sin B) and C ≡ (a,0)</p>\n<p>Now consider l(CA) = b</p>\n<p>∴ b<sup>2</sup> = (a- c cos B)<sup>2</sup> + (0-c sin B)<sup>2</sup>  , by distance formula</p>\n<p>∴ b<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> - 2 ac  cos B + c<sup>2</sup> cos<sup>2</sup> B +c<sup>2</sup> sin<sup>2</sup> B</p>\n<p>∴ b<sup>2</sup> =a<sup>2</sup> -2 ac  cos B +c<sup>2</sup> (sin<sup>2</sup>B + cos<sup>2</sup>B)</p>\n<p>∴ b<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> +c<sup>2</sup> - 2 ac cos B</p>\n<p>Hence proved.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077e1","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077e1","q":"<p> In , ΔABC with usual notations prove that</p>\n<p>(a-b)<sup>2</sup> cos<sup>2</sup> `(\"C\"/2) +(\"a\"+\"b\")^2 \"sin\"^2(\"C\"/2) = \"c\"^2`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Taking LHS </p>\n<p>= `(\"a\"-\"b\")^2 \"cos\"^2 \"C\"/2 + (\"a\"+\"b\")^2 \"sin\"^2 \"C\"/2`</p>\n<p>`=(\"a\"^2+\"b\"^2 -2\"ab\") \"cos\"^2\"C\"/2 +(\"a\"^2 +\"b\"^2 +2\"ab\").\"sin\"\"C\"/2`</p>\n<p>`= (\"a\"^2+\"b\"^2)\"cos\"\"C\"/2 - 2  \"ab\"  \"cos\"^2\"C\"/2 + (\"a\"^2+\"b\"^2) . \"sin\"^2\"C\" /2 + 2  \"ab\"  \"sin\"^2 \"C\"/2`</p>\n<p>`=(\"a\"^2 + \"b\"^2)(\"cos\"^2\"C\"/2 +\"sin\"^2\"C\"/2) - 2\"ab\"(\"cos\"^2\"C\"/2 - \"sin\"^2\"C\"/2)`</p>\n<p>=`(\"a\"^2 +\"b\"^2) -2\"ab\"  \"cos\"\"C\"`             {By cosine Rule}</p>\n<p>= c<sup>2</sup></p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077ab","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077ab","q":"<p>In `triangle ABC` prove that `tan((C-A)/2) = ((c-a)/(c+a))cot  B/2`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>In `triangle ABC`, by sine Rule</p>\n<p>`a/(sin A) = b/(sin B) = c/(sin C) = K`</p>\n<p>∴ a =  k sinA, b = k sinB, c = k sinC</p>\n<p>Consider,</p>\n<p>`(c-a)/(c+a) = (ksinC - ksinA)/(ksinC + ksin A)`</p>\n<p>`= (sinC - sin A)/(sin C + sin A)`</p>\n<p>`= (2cos((C+A)/2) sin((C-A)/2))/(2sin((C+A)/2)cos ((C-A)/2))`</p>\n<p>`= cot((C+A)/2)tan((C-A)/2)`</p>\n<p>`= tan  B/2 tan((C-A)/2)`</p>\n<p>`:. tan((C-A)/2) = ((C-a)/(C+a)) cot  B/2`</p>\n<p>Hence proved</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077b0","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077b0","q":"<p>Prove that `sin^(-1) (3/5) + cos^(-1) (12/13) = sin^(-1) (56/65)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let `cos^(-1)  12/13 = x`</p>\n<p>∴ `cos x = 12/13`</p>\n<p>∴ `sin x = 5/13`</p>\n<p>and let `sin^(-1)  3/5 = y `</p>\n<p>sin y = `3/5`</p>\n<p>`:. cos y= 4/5`</p>\n<p>∴ using sin (x + y) = sin x cos y + cos x sin y</p>\n<p>`= 5/13xx4/5+ 12/13xx3/5`</p>\n<p>`= (20+36)/(13xx5)`</p>\n<p>= `56/65`</p>\n<p>∴ x + y =`sin^(-1)  56/65`</p>\n<p>`cos^(-1)  12/13 + sin^(-1)  3/5 = sin^(-1)  56/65`</p>\n<p>Hence proved.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Trigonometric Functions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"}]}